  "schema_domain_separation": "Canonical structure is distinct from tiny-reference support. Within bounded inventory, structurally valid N>17/M>3/P>8, complex request data and unsupported reference configurations yield indeterminate/unsupported_reference, not invalid_request. Candidate-local canonical field errors are known-ineligible when raw supplied content is authenticated. Global canonical request fields, duplicate IDs/content or request JSON errors are invalid_request. Missing/corrupt artifacts remain UNKNOWN.",
  "decision_precedence": [
    {
      "priority": 1,
      "condition": "malformed request envelope, canonical types, tau, duplicate IDs or duplicate complete content",
      "request_status": "invalid_request",
      "selected_id": null
    },
    {
      "priority": 2,
      "condition": "well-formed request outside tiny reference domain or resource envelope",
      "request_status": "indeterminate",
      "reason": "unsupported_reference",
      "selected_id": null
    },
    {
      "priority": 3,
      "condition": "candidate supplied bytes available and authenticated; known incompatible config, malformed array, nonfinite coefficient/rho or invalid values",
      "candidate_status": "known_ineligible",
      "continue_other_candidates": true
    },
    {
      "priority": 4,
      "condition": "missing/corrupt raw artifact, producer binding absent/corrupt, unsupported assessment, incomplete slots or resource exhaustion",
      "candidate_status": "unknown",
      "request_status": "indeterminate",
      "selected_id": null
    },
    {
      "priority": 5,
      "condition": "every required assessment completed; at least one known eligible qualifier",
      "request_status": "selected",
      "rule": "minimum (pole_count, stable_id)"
    },
    {
      "priority": 6,
      "condition": "every required assessment completed; no known eligible qualifier",
      "request_status": "no_supplied_candidate_meets_bound",
      "selected_id": null
    }
  ],
  "precedence_notes": [
    "Inventory all observable reasons, even when a higher-priority request disposition applies; incomplete assessment is never a completed rejection.",
    "Known incompatible kernel l1, method legacy, head false, N/order/dt/producer mismatch is candidate-ineligible in a valid GL/RL request; not an unsupported request.",
    "Authenticated NaN/Inf bytes in a supplied fit are known-ineligible. A missing file, bad byte count or failed digest for bytes claimed to be a complete raw artifact is UNKNOWN. An explicitly supplied array with invalid rank/shape is known malformed, not missing.",
    "The EXHAUSTIVE completeness policy mandates indeterminate for any unknown lower OR higher rank. A higher unknown cannot displace an already established lower mathematical minimum; policy nevertheless withholds selection. This is stricter than minimum-rank inference.",
    "An input integrity failure (missing/corrupt request input artifact) is global indeterminate, not numerical evidence. Request syntax/type errors are invalid_request.",
    "An unsupported finite problem is not mathematically invalid and does not narrow public support. Empty candidate list is invalid_request; 9..32 inventoried candidates are unsupported_reference; over 32 or over input-byte limits is input_envelope_exceeded/indeterminate without promising unlimited ID inventory.",
    "Any required missing producer evidence keeps assessment UNKNOWN even with locally observed configuration incompatibility; retain both reasons. Duplicate supplied ID and complete content retain both reasons and supplied occurrences. No ID uniqueness coercion in invalid raw input."
  ],
  "identity": {
    "id_regex": "^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$",
    "id_comparison": "unsigned ASCII bytes, case-sensitive, no locale/Unicode normalization",
